<ui:UXML xmlns:ui="UnityEngine.UIElements" editor-extension-mode="False">
    <Style src="../Common/theme.uss" />
    <Style src="../MainMenu/mainmenu.uss" />
    <!--
      Account creation, as a SCENE (Sam, 2026-08-25). The sign-in gate and the name/password step
      were two `.mm-modal` overlays inside MainMenuScreen.uxml until then. Same call character
      creation got, and the Store before it: full-screen, opaque, unskippable, a destination.

      WHY IT HAD TO MOVE, AND WHY "IT ALREADY WAS A ROW" WAS NOT ENOUGH. mainmenu.uss records a
      2026-08-23 measurement that split the pitch from the form because "the gate lands near 276dp
      and the name modal near 358dp, against 411 available" (pre-#349 units, when the panel was
      914 x 411 rather than today's 2400 x 1080). The budget in that sentence is wrong even in its
      own units:
      both modals carried `.emb-bleed`, which pads by the `edge-safe` var — 52dp PER EDGE — and
      `git merge-base` (is-ancestor) confirms `.emb-bleed` was already on them when it was written.
      The real box was 411 - 104 = 307dp, so the gate fitted with 31dp to spare and THE NAME STEP
      OVERFLOWED BY 51dp. That is the step with no way past it, which is why a first launch was a
      dead end rather than a cosmetic problem.

      So re-hosting alone would not have fixed it — the nesting is the bug. As a modal the flow sat
      inside `.emb-bleed`'s 52dp per edge PLUS `.mm-modal__panel`'s `space-8` padding
      (32dp per edge) inside an already-inset box, on a panel that only has 411dp of height. Here
      the root IS the panel: one clearance, one padding, nothing nested inside it.

      EVERY ELEMENT KEEPS ITS NAME. SignInGateController takes an arbitrary root VisualElement and
      does `root.Q<>()` by name, so it is reused here completely unchanged — this file is the only
      thing that had to know the flow moved. The inner classes stay `.mm-modal__*` for the same
      reason character creation kept `character-roster.uss`: restyling them here would be a second
      source of truth for the same widgets. The two ScrollViews are gone; content that fits needs
      no scroller, and a scroller was how the overflow stayed invisible.

      NO DOUBLE HYPHEN ANYWHERE IN THIS COMMENT. XML forbids it inside a comment, so a CSS custom
      property written out in full (var, open paren, two hyphens) makes the whole file unparseable.
      Unity does not report it: rootVisualElement comes back empty, the controller logs
      "No rootVisualElement", and the screen is simply blank. Name the var without its prefix.
    -->
    <ui:VisualElement name="root" class="emb-root account-create-screen emb-bleed">

        <!-- SIGN IN: email, then the six-digit code that arrives in the reply. No Cancel, no Skip
             and no guest — Sam's 2026-08-08 ruling. The only way out is a session, so this view
             deliberately has nothing that dismisses it. -->
        <!-- TWO ROWS, and every element as high up the panel as it will go (Sam, 2026-08-30). Both
             views own a text field, so the IME is open here more often than not, and on the Pixel 5a
             its top edge lands at roughly 119dp of the 411dp panel. A tall single column puts the
             thing you are typing into, and the button that accepts it, underneath the keyboard.
             Row 1 carries the question and the answer; row 2 carries everything secondary. -->
        <ui:VisualElement name="signin-view">
            <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__columns mm-row">
                <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__pitch">
                    <ui:Label name="signin-title" text="Create your account" class="mm-modal__title"/>
                    <ui:Label name="signin-help" text="Emberfall needs an account before you can play. Enter your email and we will send you a six-digit code." class="mm-modal__help"/>
                </ui:VisualElement>
                <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__form">
                    <!-- THE FORK, and it is the first thing a launch with no session sees. Both
                         branches end at the same Supabase identity, so this is not two auth systems;
                         what it changes is what happens AFTER. A returning player is asked for a
                         password rather than sent to their inbox, is never asked to choose a
                         "permanent" display name a second time, and has this device's collection
                         scope bound to the account they just proved they own. Before it existed
                         there was no way to say "I have been here before", so every launch was
                         treated as a first one. -->
                    <ui:VisualElement name="signin-choice" class="mm-modal__actions">
                        <ui:Button name="btn-signin-new" text="I am new here" class="mm-modal__button mm-modal__button--cta"/>
                        <ui:Button name="btn-signin-returning" text="I have an account" class="mm-modal__button"/>
                    </ui:VisualElement>
                    <ui:TextField name="signin-email" class="mm-modal__field"/>
                    <ui:TextField name="signin-password" password="true" class="mm-modal__field" style="display: none;"/>
                    <ui:TextField name="signin-code" max-length="6" class="mm-modal__field mm-signin__code" style="display: none;"/>
                    <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__actions">
                        <ui:Button name="btn-signin-back" text="Use another email" class="mm-modal__button" style="display: none;"/>
                        <ui:Button name="btn-signin-primary" text="Email me a code" class="mm-modal__button mm-modal__button--cta"/>
                    </ui:VisualElement>
                </ui:VisualElement>
            </ui:VisualElement>
            <ui:VisualElement class="mm-row mm-row--secondary">
                <ui:Label name="signin-error" text=" " class="mm-modal__error"/>
                <ui:Button name="btn-signin-resend" text="Send another code" class="mm-signin__resend" style="display: none;"/>
                <!-- The password was always OPTIONAL (NOR-246), so a returning player may well not
                     have one. This is their way through and it must never be hidden on the password
                     step, or that step is a dead end for exactly the players it was built for. -->
                <ui:Button name="btn-signin-code-instead" text="Email me a code instead" class="mm-signin__resend" style="display: none;"/>
                <ui:Label name="signin-or" text="or" class="mm-signin__or"/>
                <ui:Button name="btn-signin-google" text="Continue with Google" class="mm-modal__button mm-signin__google"/>
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

        <!-- NAME: the display name, and optionally a password. First run is the only run that ever
             reaches this (NOR-287): a display name is permanent, so there is no second caller and
             no Cancel — there is no earlier name to fall back to. The password is offered here and
             only here (NOR-246), because this is the one moment the player already holds a live
             session to attach one to. -->
        <ui:VisualElement name="name-view">
            <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__columns mm-row">
                <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__pitch">
                    <ui:Label name="name-title" text="What should we call you?" class="mm-modal__title"/>
                    <ui:Label name="name-help" text="This is the name other players see. Choose carefully — it is permanent. To change it later you would have to contact support." class="mm-modal__help"/>
                </ui:VisualElement>
                <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__form">
                    <ui:TextField name="name-field" max-length="16" class="mm-modal__field"/>
                    <ui:VisualElement class="mm-modal__actions">
                        <ui:Button name="btn-name-confirm" text="Continue" class="mm-modal__button mm-modal__button--cta"/>
                    </ui:VisualElement>
                </ui:VisualElement>
            </ui:VisualElement>
            <!-- ROW 2. The password is optional and AccountCreateController shows or hides these
                 three by name, so they must keep their names and may not be nested any deeper than
                 a Q() from the root will reach — which is any depth, but the names are the contract. -->
            <ui:VisualElement class="mm-row mm-row--secondary">
                <ui:Label name="name-password-help" text="Optional: set a password so you can sign back in without checking your email." class="mm-modal__help" style="display: none;"/>
                <ui:TextField name="name-password" password="true" class="mm-modal__field" style="display: none;"/>
                <ui:TextField name="name-password-confirm" password="true" class="mm-modal__field" style="display: none;"/>
                <ui:Label name="name-error" text=" " class="mm-modal__error"/>
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

    </ui:VisualElement>
</ui:UXML>
